  "term": "problem behavior",
  "definition": "Problem behavior refers to maladaptive behavior in adolescents that interferes with social adjustment. It tends to become more common during adolescence and can affect functioning at home, school, and in the community, with examples including aggression, rule-breaking, and social withdrawal.",
